-- title:
--   From an Ogg translate profile to a branch-labelling unit
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity ($\mathtt{h\xi}$), and assume `hι`: there is a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L(\!(t)\!)$ which by `hK` equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q * ℓ) ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q * ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is: the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(t)\!)$ generated by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb Q$ of the modular curve of level $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ attached to the subgroup [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q * ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) of $(\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times$, the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field, an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ the fraction field of $A$, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that on $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) (`hj`), the coefficientwise image of the rational $j$-expansion $t^{-1}\cdot\sum$, let $\varpi$ be a generator of $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A ↥K j` for $j$ viewed in $C$.
--
--   The point of the special fibre is given by: a maximal ideal $y$ of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j_0\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Further: a point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the spectra of the two chart algebras along the middle chart), the germ $\varpi z$ at $z$ of the global function on $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ through the structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}A$ (`hϖz`), assumed to lie in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$ (`hz`); a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ with `ιFin` sending $y'$ to $z$ (`hy'`), satisfying the same supersingularity condition (`hss'`) and with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}=y$ (`hy'y`).
--
--   The Drinfeld chart witness at $z$ consists of: a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$ which is a domain, a ring homomorphism $\sigma_1\colon A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), power series $f_1,u_1,v_1\in W_1[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`, the right-hand side being [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₁`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e_1$ from the completion of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ along its maximal ideal onto $S=W_1[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1)$. Throughout, $\mathrm{toC}$ denotes the map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY}$ the canonical homomorphism $C\to\mathcal O_{X,z}$ determined by $y'$; and for $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$, saying that $\tau\colon K\simeq_L K$ satisfies [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q * ℓ) ξ (q * ℓ) ((q * ℓ) ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q * ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) means that for all weights $k$, all pairs of modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on the level subgroup attached to $N_0$ and `levelH (q * ℓ) M'` with integral $q$-expansions and $g$ nonzero, all $x\in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the quotient of those $q$-expansions, and all $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, the series $\iota(\tau x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k\mathtt{conjElemN}(q\ell)(\gamma^{-1})$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k\mathtt{conjElemN}(q\ell)(\gamma^{-1})$; such a $\tau$ is called below the level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hW₁` is a conjunction of seven clauses, grouped and summarised here as follows. (a) Compatibility with the base: for every $a\in A$, $e_1$ carries the image in the completion of the germ at $z$ of the function coming from $a$ to $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1a))$. (b) Stability of the chart: every level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ maps $C$ into $C$. (c) Triviality modulo $y'$ at level $\ell$: if moreover $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$. (d) Matrix description: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W_1$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W_1)$ such that $\theta$ intertwines the two maps $C\to S$ given by $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ and by the same map precomposed with $\tau$, $\theta$ fixes every constant $\mathrm{mkS}(C(w))$, $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}(X_j))\equiv\mathrm{mkS}\big(\sum_iC(M_{ij})X_i\big)$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, $c^{q+1}\equiv1$ and $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$, $c\equiv1$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and $c\not\equiv1$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity of $K$. (e) Separation of branches: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting at least one of $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, each containing $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$, and each containing an element $\mathrm{mkS}(C(a_i)X_0+C(b_i)X_1+h)$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and of $P_2$ along $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}$ are distinct ideals of the stalk. (f) Recognition by Laurent coefficients: for a prime $P$ of $S$ omitting at least one of $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, containing $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$ and containing an element $\mathrm{mkS}(C(1)X_0+C(0)X_1+h)$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a\in C$ satisfies $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))\in e_1^{-1}(P)$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$, viewed in $L(\!(t)\!)$, lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$. (g) A normalised branch datum: the rescaled $j$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q * ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0\in A$ with the difference of that element and the image of $a_0$ in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, an integer $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b\in W_1$ not both in $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ the element $\sum_{i\le e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e_1$ sends the image under $\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ of that difference to $\mathrm{mkS}(h)$.
--
--   Finally, let $g\in C$ be nonzero as an element of $K$ (`hg0`) such that: (`hgϖ`) $g$ divides a power of $\varpi$ in $C$, i.e. $g\,z=(\text{image of }\varpi)^k$ for some $k\in\mathbb N$ and $z\in C$; (`hginv`) $\tau g=g$ for every $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$; and (`hgprof`, the translate profile) for every $\delta\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\delta^{-1}$, all Laurent coefficients of $\tau g$ lie in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ in $L$ if and only if $q\nmid\delta_{10}$. Let $\mathfrak p$ be a prime ideal of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$, with $\mathfrak p\le y$ and $\mathfrak p\ne y$.
--
--   Then there exists $u\in C$, nonzero as an element of $K$, such that: $u$ divides a power of $\varpi$ in $C$, that is $u\,z=(\text{image of }\varpi)^k$ for some $k\in\mathbb N$ and $z\in C$; $\tau u=u$ for every $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$; $u\notin\mathfrak p$; and $u\in\mathfrak p'$ for every prime ideal $\mathfrak p'$ of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$ with $\mathfrak p'\le y$, $\mathfrak p'\ne y$ and $\mathfrak p'\ne\mathfrak p$.
--
--   The statement converts an element of the $j$-finite chart algebra whose behaviour under the Hecke-style translates $\delta\in\Gamma_0(M')$ is governed by the lower-left entry of $\delta$ modulo $q$ into a unit labelling a single one of the branches (Igusa components) through the supersingular point $y$: invertible along $\mathfrak p$ and vanishing along all the other primes of the special fibre below $y$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_labelUnit_chartAlgFin_of_end_blowupChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_labelUnit_chartAlgFin_of_end_blowupChart).
